    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 31</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="254" ed="#liebermann"/>K. Wutan eac ealle ymbe friþes bote ⁊ ymbe feos bote smeagean swyðe georne:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete"><pb n="254" ed="#liebermann"/>Wytan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#VIAtr_31.lnote.oe.4"/> eac ealle ymbe friðes bote ⁊ ymbe féos bote smeagan swiðe georne:</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="31" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="100" ed="#robertson"/>Wutan eac ealle ymbe friþes bote ⁊ ymbe feos bote smeagean swyðe georne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="172" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Wutan eac ealle ymbe friþes bote and ymbe feos bote smeagean swyðe georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="255" ed="#liebermann"/>Lasst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_31.lnote.de.1"/> uns auch alle auf Besserung öffentlicher Sicherheit und auf Besserung der Münze recht ernsthaft bedacht sein:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Let us also all very earnestly consider the improvement of public security and the improvement of the coinage:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_31.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="101" ed="#robertson"/>Further, let us all earnestly take thought for the promotion of public security and the improvement of the coinage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="173" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Let us all also consider very carefully the enhancement of public safety and the improvement of the currency.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="255"><ref target="clause:VAtr_26-1">V Atr 26.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 26, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_8">II Cn 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="344"><label>parallel (VI version)</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_26-1">V Atr 26.1–30</ref> <quote>n. 374: V Atr 26:1 – 30 (VI 31 – 37, 34 on damage to ships is new)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>source in V–VIII Æthelred</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-055">Cn 1018 20–20.2</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: VI Æthelred 31–32.1 | D 20–20.2 | II Cnut 8</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_8">II Cn 8</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 8: Cn 1018 20-20:2 (HomN L) VI Atr 31-32:1  III Eg 8</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIAtr_31.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">254</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">grosse Initiale</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">large initial</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_31.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">benutzt durch II Cn 8—10; und 31—32, 2 durch <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 271f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">used by II Cn 8—10; and 31—32, 2 by <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 271f.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">On several rubrics: VI Atr 31—32, 3</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_31.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">334</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. V, 26, 1; II Cn. 8.</seg></note>
      </div>
